    "Store the external provider in CachedAuth under the same inner RwLock as credentials, credential revision and scoped permanent failure.",
    "Resolve/classify and prepare external persistence before installation; publish provider plus prepared credentials and clear prior-source failure under one owner write guard.",
    "Private AuthOwnerUpdate::Install requires prepared credentials and cannot represent Preserve; cache-only updates retain the selected source.",
    "Clear checks source presence and clears its provider/cache/failure within one guard; absent external source preserves native state.",
    "Retired provider/auth/failure/revision values are owned until after policy and credential guards are dropped; existing notification semantics and workload ownership rules remain compatible.",
    "The legacy provider projection returns None for a poisoned owner; checked acquisition remains unavailable and an owned install reports a transient failure."
  ],
  "limits": [
    "Narrow paired in-memory source/credential/failure publication and retirement prerequisite; install uses CachePolicy::Unfenced.",
    "No installer admission ordering, pending-install-after-clear arbitration, retained source identity/ABA fencing, or coherent source/cache/policy capture. Equal-byte source replacement clears prior-source failure without advancing credential revision.",
    "Refresh success can still overwrite a newer source pair; outer refresh failure ownership remains separate. Cache-only commit and conditional model-cache publication are not source fences.",
